# Body Copy Typography — `text-body-copy`

When a client reports **paragraph text too small on mobile/tablet**, use the shared utility in `src/app/globals.css`. Do **not** change `html { font-size }` — that inflates all `em`-based headings, gaps, and image heights site-wide.

## Utility scale

| Viewport | Size |
|----------|------|
| Mobile (&lt;768px) | 14px (`0.875rem`) |
| Tablet (768–1439px) | 16px (`1rem`) |
| Desktop (≥1440px) | `0.72em` (scales with root) |

## When to apply

Replace `text-[0.72em]` (or similar small `em` body sizes) on **paragraphs only**:

```tsx
// BAD — ~10px on mobile (0.72 × 14px root)
<p className="font-ui text-[0.72em] leading-[1.4] ...">

// GOOD
<p className="font-ui text-body-copy leading-[1.4] ...">
```

Keep `leading`, `tracking`, color, and `font-ui` / `font-body` unchanged.

